  "body": "Found while working #995 (PR #1034).\n\n**What is wrong.** #574 made every built-in mill post state its spindle stopped (M5; MOTOFF on Mazak) after a touch probe's tool change and length offset, before its first move - so a control whose tool change leaves the spindle turning (a same-tool continuation, a manual change) still brings the probe to the part stopped. `doosan-dnm.cps` (#614, added after #574) has no such block: its `startPreamble` skips S/M3 for a section with a stated speed of 0 but writes no M5. `crates/app/tests/probe_spindle_stop.rs` lists every mill post except `doosan-dnm`, so nothing catches it.\n\nWhy P2: the Doosan's M6 stops the spindle on a normal tool change, so it bites only on a same-tool continuation; no gouge, but a turning probe is a broken probe.\n\nDone means: `doosan-dnm` writes M5 between a probe section's tool change / G43 and its first move, and `doosan-dnm` joins `MILL_POSTS` in `probe_spindle_stop.rs` (both of its tests).",
